;; Authored collections of tags and metadata for block-type entity specs.
;; Depends on 1-tags.edn and, for data validation, the future agent model.
;;
;; Concrete block types are separately authored native entity-spec entities:
;; db/ident + block-type/title + author + db.entity/attrs and/or
;; db.entity/preds. Their required/singular tag sets are additional metadata.
;; A block/type refers to one of these concrete blueprints, not block/validate.
;; Writers ensure BOTH block/validate and the selected concrete blueprint.
;; The generic predicate does not automatically execute other blueprint specs.
;;
;; Schema-only draft: the named native predicates are not implemented/registered.
;; They must be deployed before these specs can be successfully ensured.
;; Required/singular metadata is a validation contract, not a native EDB trigger.
;; Type changes and child edits require explicit validation of affected parents.
;; Shared tags are live refs: edit intentionally for all users, or replace the
;; membership with a new assignment for a local change. Preserve fact history.
[
 {:db/ident :block-type/title
  :db/valueType :db.type/string
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
  :db/doc "Nonempty human-readable name of an authored block blueprint, for example Worked example. The same entity has a db/ident, author, and native entity-spec facts. It is not a second entity wrapping the spec. Ensure block-type/validate when authoring it."}

 {:db/ident :block-type/required-tag-types
  :db/valueType :db.type/ref
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many
  :db/doc "Tag types that must each occur at least once in a block using this blueprint. Targets are the native answer attribute entities defined as tag types, not tag instances. Absence imposes no additional required types; it does not prohibit tags. Combine with singular-tag-types to require exactly one assignment of a type. Extra valid tag types remain allowed."}

 {:db/ident :block-type/singular-tag-types
  :db/valueType :db.type/ref
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many
  :db/doc "Tag types allowed at most once in a block using this blueprint. A type only in this set is optional; a type also in required-tag-types must occur exactly once. Types outside this set may have multiple distinct tag assignments. This constrains tag instances by type, independently of the native answer attribute's cardinality inside each tag."}

 {:db/ident :block/id
  :db/valueType :db.type/uuid
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
  :db/unique :db.unique/identity
  :db/doc "Stable identity of an authored collection of tags. Independent of its placement in hyperdocs; a reused block keeps its identity and its own authorship."}

 {:db/ident :block/type
  :db/valueType :db.type/ref
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
  :db/doc "Concrete authored native entity spec defining this block's blueprint. Must satisfy block-type/validate. This ordinary ref does not own the shared type or automatically invoke its rules. Writers explicitly ensure the generic block spec and this selected spec on every relevant write."}

 {:db/ident :block/tags
  :db/valueType :db.type/ref
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many
  :db/doc "Unordered collection of authored tag assignments. Ordinary refs permit deliberate reuse and preserve tags when a block is removed. The block's single author assembled the collection; each tag retains its own single author. Validate each tag and the collection's required/singular type rules. This relationship supplies reverse lookup of containing blocks; do not maintain duplicate tag-to-block membership. Editing a shared tag affects every current referring block."}

 {:db/ident :block-type/validate
  :db.entity/attrs [:db/ident :block-type/title :author]
  :db.entity/preds course-academy.generics/valid-block-type?
  :db/doc "Strict block-blueprint contract. The future predicate checks a nonempty title, one valid author agent, an actual native entity spec with required attrs and/or predicates, and valid tag-type targets in both rule sets. The sets may overlap and may be absent. Schema metadata remains open to additional facts. Ensuring the blueprint does not retroactively validate blocks that use it."}

 {:db/ident :block/validate
  :db.entity/attrs [:block/id :block/type :block/tags :author]
  :db.entity/preds course-academy.generics/valid-block?
  :db/doc "Strict complete-block contract requiring identity, a concrete blueprint, one or more tags, and exactly one valid author agent. The future predicate checks the blueprint and complete child tags, then counts assignments by tag/type to enforce required and singular sets in the proposed database. It does not interpret tag order or reject unrelated metadata. Writers also ensure the selected native blueprint spec to execute any additional native requirements/predicates, and ensure edited children and affected hyperdocs. No automatic recursive or ongoing constraint is created."}
]
